{"summary":"Both amendments identify real regressions: one is a broken, index-coupled TUI test, and the other is a save-migration semantic change that silently alters queued trim behavior.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-5f3aaec6","decision":"accept","rationale":"The current test is demonstrably wrong: after inserting `TrimPlantsAndLeaveCuttings` into `ActionKind::ALL`, advancing 5 times lands on `CleanFilter`, so the test no longer exercises integer count validation at all. Fixing the navigation count, or better selecting `ActionKind::AddShrimp` directly, restores the intended coverage and removes brittle dependence on enum ordering."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-d613a3c7","decision":"accept","rationale":"The migration currently rewrites legacy `TrimPlants` to `TrimPlantsAndRemove`, which changes queued-action behavior from keeping trimmed biomass in-system to exporting it. Historical code and routing docs show legacy `TrimPlants` behaved as the in-tank variant, so this is a real save-compatibility bug; even if the exact preservation path needs nuance, the amendment correctly identifies an unsafe silent semantic change that should be fixed or explicitly documented as intentional."}]}